\f0\fs24 \cf0 Units and Types\
From a user\'92s perspective, every variable must have a specified unit basis and type (e.g. \'93seconds\'94, \'93integer\'94), and these must match in such a way that the operation being performed is valid on these types. By way of example, if the user wants to evaluate x < y, where x is in seconds and y is in kilograms, this is an invalid comparison. A user 
\f1\i can
\f0\i0  label a value as unitless, but this must be done explicitly.\
GORP: What is it?\
GORP (Gestalt Object Relational Programming) is a non-Turing Complete language for working with \
GORP Primitives\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}And\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Choose\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Compare\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Equal\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Exists\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Filter\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Forall\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Greater\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}If\
